<VI _name="eDyno Accel Synth.vi" description="Synthesizes one block of eDyno drivetrain acceleration (g) as seen by a PCB 356A15 ICP accelerometer (one axis) on an e-bike motor housing.\0A\0ASpeed ramps linearly from rpm start to rpm end across the block\2C and every order tracks speed. Shaft phase (revolutions) and the sample counter travel in State in/State out: feed State out back into State in through a shift register in the caller so consecutive blocks are phase-continuous.\0A\0ABaseline: a small 1x residual plus broadband noise. Injectable faults (Fault Injection cluster):\0A- Imbalance: 1x order\2C amplitude scales with (rpm/ref)^2\0A- Misalignment: 2x order\0A- Bearing outer race (BPFO): impacts every 1/(BPFO order x shaft Hz) ringing the housing resonance with exponential decay\0A- Motor torque ripple: 6 x pole-pairs order\0A- Inverter PWM: carrier with sidebands at carrier +/- 2 x electrical frequency\0A\0AFault Frequencies returns the expected frequencies at rpm end\2C for the engineer to check against the spectrum. Speed (rpm) returns the instantaneous shaft speed per sample\2C and Tach Pulse 1ppr a 50 % duty once-per-rev square wave whose rising edge is at shaft angle 0 - both phase-locked to Accel (g) for order analysis.">
